all right firefighters in Southern  California are battling two new  wildfires that broke out this morning a  wildfire in San Bernardino is growing  fast and threatening buildings and a  fast-moving fire in Riverside County has  already burned at least two homes these  are live pictures crews faced a major  battle yesterday in Simi Valley  northwest of Los Angeles the flames came  dangerously close to the rung Reagan  Presidential Library and two nearby  neighborhoods about 30 thousand people  were forced to evacuate Carter Evans is  in Moorpark California Carter what do  you see there  well good morning this pink fire  retardant that you see here is really a  big line of defense for these homes  there are still more than a thousand  firefighters working this fire and these  high winds that are expected to continue  until this evening flames raged into the  night fueled by wind gusts up to 70  miles per hour this fire in Simi Valley  ignited just before dawn Wednesday  coming within feet of the Reagan Library  which houses memorabilia including Air  Force One this fire is raging right now  you can see the vortex of flames and  smoke and wind blowing in our direction  just imagine what it's like for  firefighters to approach flames like  that the fire quickly consumed this barn  where volunteers help rescue animals  trapped inside one horse even seemed to  turn back to lead other horses to safety  despite an all-out assault flames still  managed to jump a freeway forcing a  nearby neighborhood to evacuate  we put everything in the car and I'm so  glad we did because by the time it  jumped at 23 freeway we only had seconds  to get off to battle numerous fires  throughout the day emergency personnel  had to evacuate some patients on  stretchers the winds were powerful  enough to knock over big rigs along this  interstate yet vigilant firefighters  kept spot fires from exploding while we  were talking to captain Anthony Romero a  spot fire popped up right next to a fire  engine  dick ative of this fires behavior huh a  bunny on a head well just like that so  what you got to maintain for us is just  constant awareness that the fires gonna  keep moving if we want to maintain our  vigilance just because it is an active  firefighter now the cause of this fire  has not yet been determined but Southern  California Edison a utility did say that  it started near one of their power lines  and it had not cut power at the time the  fire started Gail  all right thank you very much Carter  Evans
 

